  <title>Documentation | ThemeBuilder Support</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/support-site.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include("partials/site-header", { activePage: "documentation" }) %>

  <main class="document-page">
    <div class="document-heading">
      <a class="back-link" href="/">← Support home</a>
      <span class="eyebrow">THEMEBUILDER HELP CENTER</span>
      <h1>Documentation</h1>
      <p class="document-intro">A starting point for using ThemeBuilder and finding help when you need it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-layout">
      <aside class="doc-sidebar" aria-label="On this page">
        <span>ON THIS PAGE</span>
        <a href="#getting-started">Getting started</a>
        <a href="#working-with-themes">Working with themes</a>
        <a href="#dashboard">Managing your account</a>
        <a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>
        <a href="#contact-support">Contact support</a>
      </aside>
      <article class="doc-content">
        <section id="getting-started">
          <span class="article-number">01</span>
          <h2>Getting started</h2>
          <p>ThemeBuilder helps you customize the look and feel of your website. Start by signing in with the account provided to you, then open the theme or workspace you want to work on.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Open ThemeBuilder and sign in with your account credentials.</li>
            <li>Choose the website or theme you want to customize.</li>
            <li>Make your changes and preview them before applying them.</li>
            <li>Save or publish changes using the controls available in your workspace.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>Available options can vary based on your account access and the integrations enabled for your workspace.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="working-with-themes">
          <span class="article-number">02</span>
          <h2>Working with themes</h2>
          <p>Use the theme editor to adjust the visual elements available in your workspace, such as colors, typography, and layout. Preview your work as you go, and check the result at different screen sizes where preview options are available.</p>
          <div class="note-box"><strong>Tip</strong><span>Make a small change first and preview it before continuing. This makes it easier to spot which adjustment caused an unexpected result.</span></div>
        </section>

        <section id="dashboard">
          <span class="article-number">03</span>
          <h2>Managing your account</h2>
          <p>Sign-in and account access are managed by your administrator. If you can’t sign in, your account details need updating, or you believe you have the wrong access level, contact your account administrator or email support.</p>
          <p>For administrators, the dashboard provides access to agency records and related management tools. Only authorized administrators should use the admin login.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="troubleshooting">
          <span class="article-number">04</span>
          <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>A page doesn’t load:</strong> Refresh the page and check your internet connection. If the issue continues, try again later.</li>
            <li><strong>Your changes don’t appear:</strong> Confirm that your changes were saved or published, then reload the page you’re previewing.</li>
            <li><strong>You can’t sign in:</strong> Check that you’re using the correct account and contact your administrator if you need access help.</li>
            <li><strong>You see an unexpected display:</strong> Note the page, the steps you took, and the browser you’re using before contacting support.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="contact-support">
          <span class="article-number">05</span>
          <h2>Contact support</h2>
          <p>Email us with a clear description of the issue. Include the page or feature involved, what you expected to happen, and what happened instead. Please don’t include passwords or other sensitive credentials.</p>
          <a class="inline-email" href="mailto:haseebharry07@gmail.com">haseebharry07@gmail.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <%- include("partials/site-footer") %>
